 For information about possible ambiguous cases, see [options taking varying arguments](./docs/options-taking-varying-arguments.md).
 
+### Merged option values
+
+The `.optsWithGlobals()` method returns an object containing merged local and global option values as key-value pairs.
+Local option values take precedence over global option values.
+
+```js
+program
+  .option('-f, --foo', 'add some foo')
+  .option('-b, --bar', 'add some bar');
+
+const sub = program.command('sub');
+sub
+  .option('-b, --bar <bar>', 'add some bar')
+  .option('-c, --cheese <cheese>', 'add some cheese');
+
+program.parse(['node', 'test', '--foo', 'sub', '--bar', 'sub', '--cheese', 'sub']);
+
+console.log(sub.optsWithGlobals());
+// { foo: true, bar: 'sub', cheese: 'sub' }
+```
+
 ### Version option
 
 The optional `version` method adds handling for displaying the command version. The default option flags are `-V` and `--version`, and when present the command prints the version number and exits.
